                <pb facs="0947" n="841" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg841"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Minister
                    Merry.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-07-15"><hi rendition="#italic">July 15,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Bacon informs Mr. Merry that President Esealon’s message accepting agreement
                    to negotiate peace was followed by a telegram from the President of Guatemala
                    cordially accepting the President’s proposals and acquiescing in an armistice
                    being agreed to and the terms of peace being negotiated on the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Marblehead</hi>. The President rejoices that the
                    President of Mexico is also interested in the cause of peace. Mr. Bacon states
                    that it now only remains to bring the parties together, and that it is the
                    President’s wish that Mr. Merry, Mr. Combs, and the Mexican minister to Central
                    America may act in unison in every way toward a successful negotiation and that
                    all three attend on the <hi rendition="#italic">Marblehead.</hi>)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
